                   :fields {:input {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}},
   :context [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "review-task-design" :yield :text}}]}
  {:name "review-task-plan",
   :type :delegate,
   :target "review-task-plan",
   :prompt-string {:type :map,
                   :fields {:input {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}},
   :context [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "review-task-design" :yield :text}}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "create-task-plan" :yield :text}}]}
  {:name "clean-baseline",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash" "edit" "write"],
   :skills ["testing-without-mocks"],
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "review-task-design" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "create-task-plan" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "review-task-plan" :yield :text}}
    {:type :template,
     :text "Establish the pre-characterization clean-source baseline for the incidental-complexity Munera task described by {{input}}. Work only in the invoking session's current inherited worktree. Do NOT call `work-on`, create a worktree, or switch branches.\n\nRequired procedure:\n1. Read the task artifacts (`design.md`, `plan.md`, `steps.md`, `implementation.md`) and identify the target/source path(s) for the selected unit. If the target/source paths cannot be identified from the task artifacts, append a durable failure finding to task artifacts, commit that task-artifact update, and stop with `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK`.\n2. Inspect `git status --short` and verify the identified target/source paths are not already dirty before baseline recording. Pre-existing dirty task-artifact or documentation files may remain only when explicitly classified in the task artifacts; pre-existing dirty target/source changes must be appended as a durable failure finding in task artifacts, committed, and must stop the workflow instead of being absorbed into the unmodified-behavior baseline.\n3. Write `characterization-baseline.edn` in the task directory. It must include at least the recorded git `HEAD`, `git status --short`, the target/source paths identified by the task, and any explicitly classified pre-existing task-artifact-or-doc dirt.\n4. Update `implementation.md` tersely with the clean-baseline result and commit any new task-artifact update.\n5. End with exactly one line: `PASS_STATUS: REVIEW_COMPLETE` when the baseline was recorded and target/source paths were clean; otherwise `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK` only after the missing-path or dirty-path failure finding has been recorded in task artifacts and committed.\n\nInput:\n{{input}}",
     :vars {"input" {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}}],
   :judge {:type :invoke,
           :operation "workflow/pass-status-routing",
           :args {:text {:from {:step "clean-baseline" :output :final-llm-reply}},
                  :allowed-statuses ["ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK" "REVIEW_COMPLETE"]}},
   :on {"DONE" {:goto "coverage-review"},
        "REPEAT" {:goto "terminal-stop-summary"}}}
  {:name "coverage-review",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash" "edit" "write"],
   :skills ["task-test-review" "testing-without-mocks"],
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "clean-baseline" :yield :text}}
    {:type :template,
     :text "Review the pre-simplification characterization-test net for the incidental-complexity Munera task described by {{input}}. This is a Phase 0 gate before simplification. Do NOT perform simplification or refactor work. Do NOT call `work-on`; use the current inherited worktree.\n\nRequired procedure:\n1. Read the task artifacts and `characterization-baseline.edn`. Confirm the target unit and observable behavior under review are clear.\n2. Inspect existing and newly-added tests for the target's externally observable state or outputs. Cover nominal, edge, and boundary behavior relevant to the target. Follow `testing-without-mocks`: prefer state/output assertions and avoid interaction assertions unless the interaction is itself the observable behavior.\n3. Run the relevant tests needed to prove the characterization net is green against the unmodified target behavior.\n4. If coverage is sufficient and green, record the reviewed coverage and result in task artifacts, commit the task-artifact update, then end with exactly `PASS_STATUS: REVIEW_COMPLETE`.\n5. If fixable characterization gaps remain, append a new latest characterization-status note containing exactly `CHARACTERIZATION_STATUS: FIXABLE_GAPS` in the task artifacts with the concrete coverage work required, commit the task-artifact update, mention that marker and artifact path in the final response body, then end with exactly `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK`.\n6. If sufficient characterization is infeasible, append a new latest characterization-status note containing exactly `CHARACTERIZATION_STATUS: INFEASIBLE` in the task artifacts with the reason, commit the task-artifact update, mention that marker and artifact path in the final response body, and do not proceed toward simplification, then end with exactly `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK`.\n\nInput:\n{{input}}",
     :vars {"input" {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}}],
   :judge {:type :invoke,
           :operation "workflow/pass-status-routing",
           :args {:text {:from {:step "coverage-review" :output :final-llm-reply}},
                  :allowed-statuses ["ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK" "REVIEW_COMPLETE"]}},
   :on {"DONE" {:goto "diff-gate"},
        "REPEAT" {:goto "coverage-disposition"}}}
  {:name "coverage-disposition",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash" "edit" "write"],
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "coverage-review" :yield :text}}
    {:type :template,
     :text "Determine the next route for the failed characterization-test-net review for {{input}}. Read the preceding coverage-review output first, then read task artifacts only to resolve the latest committed characterization-status note that the preceding coverage review identifies. Task artifacts are append-only and may contain historical `CHARACTERIZATION_STATUS` markers from earlier coverage-review loops; stale historical markers are non-authoritative and must never override the immediately preceding coverage-review result.\n\nRouting rule, in priority order:\n1. If the immediately preceding coverage-review output mentions exactly `CHARACTERIZATION_STATUS: FIXABLE_GAPS`, report that a constrained coverage-fix pass should run and end with exactly `PASS_STATUS: REVIEW_COMPLETE`.\n2. If the immediately preceding coverage-review output mentions exactly `CHARACTERIZATION_STATUS: INFEASIBLE`, report that the workflow must stop before simplification and end with exactly `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK`.\n3. If the preceding coverage-review output does not include either marker but identifies a task-artifact path for its committed latest characterization-status note, read that artifact and use only the latest committed characterization-status note from that coverage-review commit. Route `FIXABLE_GAPS` to coverage-fix with `PASS_STATUS: REVIEW_COMPLETE`; route `INFEASIBLE` to terminal stop with `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK`.\n4. If the latest status is ambiguous, both markers appear in the immediately preceding output/latest note, neither marker is present, or only historical markers are found, append a durable coverage-disposition stop finding to task artifacts, commit that task-artifact update, and stop before simplification with exactly `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK`.\n\nWhen this step emits `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK` for an ambiguous, missing, both-marker, or stale-historical-marker disposition failure, the stop reason must be recorded in committed task artifacts before the final status line so `terminal-stop-summary` can explain the stop without relying on ephemeral coverage-disposition child-session output.\n\nDo not scan all task artifacts for any marker as the routing source. Do not let stale `FIXABLE_GAPS` or stale `INFEASIBLE` records override the latest coverage-review status. Do not edit source code. Do not perform coverage fixes here. Do not call `work-on`.\n\nInput:\n{{input}}",
     :vars {"input" {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}}],
   :judge {:type :invoke,
           :operation "workflow/pass-status-routing",
           :args {:text {:from {:step "coverage-disposition" :output :final-llm-reply}},
                  :allowed-statuses ["ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK" "REVIEW_COMPLETE"]}},
   :on {"DONE" {:goto "coverage-fix"},
        "REPEAT" {:goto "terminal-stop-summary"}}}
  {:name "coverage-fix",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash" "edit" "write"],
   :skills ["clojure-coding-standards" "testing-without-mocks"],
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "coverage-review" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "coverage-disposition" :yield :text}}
    {:type :template,
     :text "Execute only the next constrained characterization-test-net fix for the incidental-complexity Munera task described by {{input}}. This pass exists before simplification, so it may add characterization tests and explicitly justified minimal testability seams only.\n\nHard constraints:\n- Do NOT simplify, refactor, decomplect, rename, extract, reorganize, or otherwise improve the target implementation.\n- Do NOT perform unrelated cleanup.\n- Do NOT weaken existing expectations.\n- Do NOT make broad production edits. Any production change must be an explicitly justified minimal testability seam recorded in `implementation.md`.\n- Assert externally observable state or outputs; avoid interaction assertions unless the interaction is itself observable behavior.\n- Use the current inherited worktree. Do NOT call `work-on`, create a worktree, or switch branches.\n\nRequired procedure:\n1. Read the task artifacts and the latest coverage-review findings.\n2. Add/refine characterization tests for the recorded nominal, edge, or boundary gaps, or add one explicitly justified minimal testability seam if tests cannot otherwise observe behavior.\n3. Run the relevant tests and keep them green against current behavior.\n4. Update `steps.md`/`implementation.md` with what was added, including any minimal seam justification.\n5. Commit the characterization-fix changes.\n6. End with exactly `PASS_STATUS: REVIEW_COMPLETE` so coverage review runs again.\n\nInput:\n{{input}}",
     :vars {"input" {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}}],
   :judge {:type :invoke,
           :operation "workflow/pass-status-routing",
           :args {:text {:from {:step "coverage-fix" :output :final-llm-reply}},
                  :allowed-statuses ["REVIEW_COMPLETE"]}},
   :on {"DONE" {:goto "coverage-review"}}}
  {:name "diff-gate",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash" "edit" "write"],
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "clean-baseline" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "coverage-review" :yield :text}}
    {:type :template,
     :text "Run the workflow-level pre-simplification baseline/diff gate for the incidental-complexity Munera task described by {{input}}. This gate runs after characterization coverage is reviewed complete and before `implement-task`. Work in the current inherited worktree; do NOT call `work-on`, create a worktree, or switch branches.\n\nRequired procedure:\n1. Read the task artifacts and task-local `characterization-baseline.edn`. If the file is missing or lacks recorded HEAD, status, and target/source paths, stop.\n2. Verify the baseline did not include dirty target/source paths at baseline time. If it did, stop before simplification.\n3. Compare both committed changes since the baseline HEAD (`git diff <baseline-head>...HEAD` or an equivalent committed-change comparison) and the current uncommitted worktree status/diff. Coverage-fix commits must not hide coverage-phase edits behind an empty uncommitted `git diff`.\n4. Classify every coverage-phase change. Allowed categories are only: characterization tests, task artifacts, docs, and explicitly justified minimal testability seams.\n5. Stop before simplification if any change is an unclassified source/target change, broad production edit, premature simplification/refactor, missing baseline data, or `CHARACTERIZATION_STATUS: INFEASIBLE`. Record whether the change must be reverted, split, or the task closed, and commit the task-artifact update.\n6. If and only if all coverage-phase changes are allowed and relevant tests are green, record the diff-gate classification in task artifacts, commit the task-artifact update, and end with exactly `PASS_STATUS: REVIEW_COMPLETE`. Otherwise end with exactly `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK`.\n\nInput:\n{{input}}",
     :vars {"input" {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}}],
   :judge {:type :invoke,
           :operation "workflow/pass-status-routing",
           :args {:text {:from {:step "diff-gate" :output :final-llm-reply}},
                  :allowed-statuses ["ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK" "REVIEW_COMPLETE"]}},
   :on {"DONE" {:goto "implement-task"},
        "REPEAT" {:goto "terminal-stop-summary"}}}
